# Branch every push

Put every new push on its own branch. Do not push commits directly to `main` or `master`.

- Start from the latest `main`.
- Create a branch named for the work, then commit there.
- Push that branch with `-u` the first time.
- Leave `main` as it is. Opening a pull request still waits for an explicit ask.

```bash
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b servicing-school-email
git push -u origin HEAD
```
